## Development

`make help` lists every command by area. The ones used every day:

| Command | What it does |
|---|---|
| `make test` | Backend tests |
| `make lint` | Lint, format check and type check |
| `make db-migrate` | A migration from the model changes |
| `make openapi` | The API contract (`openapi/openapi.json`) from the code |
{%- if use_frontend %}
| `make client` | The contract, then the frontend client generated from it |
{%- endif %}
| `make docs-serve` | Preview the documentation |
| `make db-upgrade` / `make db-downgrade` | Apply pending migrations / roll back one |
{%- if use_jwt %}
| `make user-list` | List the users |
{%- endif %}
| `make version` | Print the project version |
| `make bump-version part=patch` | Raise the version (`patch`, `minor` or `major`) |

The version lives in one file, `VERSION`. `make bump-version` changes it and copies it into
`backend/pyproject.toml` and `frontend/package.json`, which the two images are built from;
`make lint` fails if a copy is out of step. The backend publishes it in the OpenAPI document
and the frontend shows it at the bottom of the sidebar.

